  "details": "I have discovered avatar's performance issues through many experiments and verifications.\n\nCan improvements be made in the future through replacement of constraints?\n\nIn addition, is it possible to implement two kinds of animators through script? One will use all actions only when necessary, and the other will completely eliminate or retain the transform when it is invisible.\n\nThe management of constraints and their incorrect use by a large number of players have caused many problems, which require official control and improvement alternatives.\n\nOr try to improve the single-threaded scene management API through Unity3D staff.\n\nThe animators had to keep working all the time, resulting in a certain degree of performance degradation in this area, and they were unable to effectively keep animations in sync.\n\nIt is not an exaggeration to say that these two occupy 80% of the CPU performance, and ultimately cause many problems in processing the status, transform and organization of objects.\n\nIf possible, I hope it can be solved in SDK4.0.\n\nLooking forward to official efforts.",
